      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree; when I\u0027d come back to this from my old hacky CL I was similarly confused by ensureTexturable() for a moment. It now takes GrSurfaceProxyView and SkIRect as a parameters and returns a std::pair\u003cGrSurfaceProxyView, SkIRect\u003e. Call sites just use std::tie() to update and then check that texView isn\u0027t null.\n\nI\u0027d tried using rvalues and std::move() but it seemed that using `std::tie(texView, srcRect) \u003d ensureTexturable(std::move(texView), srcRect)` confused clang-tidy and it didn\u0027t realize that `texView` had been re-assigned to after the move. I figured the compiler could remove all the redundant copies anyways on release builds, so this was cleaner than adding clang-tidy suppression comments.",
      "parentUuid": "1d21fb6d_c9c97232",
      "revId": "d445e6dfc2b0afa5465e05725912913fba6198e8",
